  url = {https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009292030},
  note = {SUMMARY: A volume of new essays on how law and morality relate in Kant: whether law is an application of general moral principles to legal institutions or has its own normativity irreducible to morality. The essays treat the justification of legal coercion, freedom and autonomy in law and politics, legal punishment and its ethical presuppositions, moral luck and permissive laws (publisher abstract).

